 "notes": ["The input is the bytes of one file, named plain.env. The entry point reads it in the grammar-only mode: the rules of a .env, no catalog and no reference.","An accepted vector holds each key of the file and its value in value.","A refused vector holds a list of faults in refusal, in the order of the reader. A fault is an object with four keys: fault, file, line and key. line 0 means the whole file, and an empty key means no key. A fault holds no value."],
